PTLib 2.10.9 (H.323 stack): include <termios.h> instead of <termio.h>

glibc 2.42 removed the legacy System V <termio.h> header, so this translation
unit does not compile on any host carrying it (Ubuntu 25.10 and newer, Debian
trixie and newer).  <termios.h> is the POSIX replacement and is what the file
already relies on in every other configuration: nothing in pipechan.cxx or the
common implementation it includes references a struct termio, only termios.

The guard around the include is upstream's and is left exactly as it is - note
that its __GLIBC_ spelling is a typo for __GLIBC__ and therefore never true on
Linux, which is why the include is dead code in practice.  It is repaired rather
than deleted because a host where the guard DOES fire must still compile.

Applies to: c01afdc78cc4fb56e497b04aea69ef575fc53bf0 (tag v2_10_9_6)
Upstream:   https://github.com/willamowius/ptlib.git

diff --git a/src/ptlib/unix/pipechan.cxx b/src/ptlib/unix/pipechan.cxx
